Z||000000||crash||10-09-2001||10:11 AM||||I am new to the forum as a user but have been reading it for a long time.<BR>My queston is if It is possible to put a b&m shifter inside a fiero?<BR>Or any other kind of aftermarket heavy duty shifter?<BR>thks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fix||10-09-2001||04:59 PM||||Allow me to be the first to say welcome to the forum.  It's always nice to see another Michigander.  Especially in the GR area. As for you're question, I'm not exactly sure.  Anything can be done with enough modifying, but usually an after market shifter assembly is made to connect thru the floor to the tranny shift linkage.  Since the fiero uses cables to shift you will run into a problem there.  Like I said, I'm sure it could be made to work if you put some effort into it, but I really don't think it would be worth it.  Anybody else?<P>------------------<BR>"If it doesn't scare you, it's not fast enough."||||reg||1
Z||000002||crash||10-11-2001||09:42 AM||||thanks for the welcome. I still think I am going to give it a shot. If it doesn't work I will use it on my fathers gto.<BR>If anyone has more info it would be greatly appreciated<BR>||||reg||1
